control_edit.py adapts the line-ending detection/normalization functions from
src/utils/lineEndingHandler.ts and exact-match/count/replacement logic from
src/tools/edit.ts. The Python adaptation preserves the MIT copyright and
permission notice. Changes: no fuzzy write, UI, tracking, or logging; bounded
replacement count, SHA-256 preconditions in the caller, BOM preservation,
overlapping-match rejection, and MCP-Local path/access guards.

Filesystem, search, and process/session APIs were reviewed as design references.
Those Windows/Python integration modules are original MCP-Local implementations
because the existing read-only guards and AppContainer isolation are required.
No Hosted Relay, account system, remote backend, telemetry, Node dependency tree,
or upstream executable is redistributed or executed by MCP-Local.
